Cross-package alias identity: repo.Lookup returns repo.ErrNotFound (var ErrNotFound = kverr.ErrNotFound) and the handler clears it with err == kverr.ErrNotFound.
Expect: 1 entry, sentinel engine.ErrClosed; neither kverr.ErrNotFound nor repo.ErrNotFound.
ErrClosed is reassigned in the engine's func init(), so errtrace treats its value as unknown: the entry is kept with two 'possibly handled'
notes ("may be the same value as kverr.ErrNotFound"), one per guard. At run time it can never equal ErrNotFound; the notes are the
documented conservative rule for unstable sentinels (plan P07, e2e guards/eq_unstable_sentinel), not a wrong set.
-- args --
api/api.go:@hfind
